    {
      "id": "swept_limit",
      "status": "EXISTING_INDEPENDENT_EVIDENCE_RECONFIRMED_BY_ALGEBRA",
      "finding": "For a straight swept bound line, all collinear bound segments have zero principal-value velocity. The trailing ray kernel contains an even sweep term sin(Lambda)/|y-eta| in addition to the odd1/(y-eta) term. Nonzero circulation gradient generates logarithmic local growth; smooth one-mode circulation already reproduces it. This rules out neighboring-bound deletion or reduced Fourier count as a general resolution.",
      "derivation": "K(y,eta)=[1/(y-eta)+sin(Lambda)/abs(y-eta)]/(4*pi); w_sweep(y;eps)=-sin(Lambda)*Gamma_prime(y)*log(1/eps)/(2*pi)+O(1).",
